# SPDX-License-Identifier: MPL-2.0
# Adjustfile — Accessibility drift-tolerance contract for progblocks
# Author: Jonathan D.A. Jewell (hyperpolymath)
#
# Cumulative-drift catchment for accessibility specifically: tolerance
# bands + corrective actions. Authority: advisory — continue-with-warnings,
# not a hard gate.

@abstract:
Accessibility is this repo's stated target (README.md: "WCAG 2.1 AA target
for all interactive elements") and its most concrete drift risk: it is easy
to let a claim of AAA, or of AA fully met, creep into documentation that
the markup does not back up. AAA IS NOT MET. AA is the target, and AA is
not fully met either — see the gaps below, all sourced from a direct read
of src/prog-block.js and src/prog-block.css on 2026-08-07.
@end

## Level Honesty

### wcag-level-honesty
- description: README states a WCAG 2.1 AA target; nothing in this repo may ASSERT AAA conformance. The pattern matches claim-shaped phrases only, so honest disclaimers ("not the previously-claimed AAA") do not trip it.
- run: "! grep -qiE '(conform|complian|meets|achiev|certif|level)[a-z]* +(to +|with +)?(wcag +)?2?\.?1? *AAA|WCAG *2?\.?1? *AAA +(conforman|complian)' README.md"
- severity: critical
- enforced-by: not yet automated (documentary)

### present-aria-semantics
- description: The baseline ARIA that IS present must not regress — role=tablist/tab and aria-selected are the floor
- run: grep -q 'role="tablist"' src/prog-block.js && grep -q 'aria-selected' src/prog-block.js
- severity: warning
- enforced-by: not yet automated (documentary)

## Known AA Gaps (tracked, not gated — do not let these silently become "compliant" claims)

### roving-tabindex-missing
- description: The tablist has no roving tabindex / arrow-key navigation, which real APG tablist semantics require for AA
- tolerance: known gap, tracked here; 0 tolerance for a documentation claim of "APG-compliant" tablist while this is open
- corrective: implement roving tabindex plus ArrowLeft/ArrowRight handling on the variant tablist
- severity: advisory

### tabpanel-pairing-missing
- description: No tabpanel role + aria-controls/aria-labelledby pairing between tabs and their content
- tolerance: known gap, tracked here
- corrective: add role="tabpanel" to variant content containers and wire aria-controls/aria-labelledby to the corresponding tab
- severity: advisory

### aria-live-missing
- description: No aria-live region for variant switches or export-state changes — a screen-reader user gets no announcement when content changes
- tolerance: known gap, tracked here
- corrective: add a polite aria-live region and update it on variant switch and on export completion
- severity: advisory

### inactive-tab-contrast
- description: Inactive tabs render at opacity: 0.7, which degrades text contrast below what AA requires at small sizes
- run: grep -q 'opacity: 0.7' src/prog-block.css
- severity: warning
- enforced-by: not yet automated (documentary)

### focus-destroyed-on-keystroke
- description: Editing any variable input triggers a full shadowRoot.innerHTML rewrite, destroying and recreating the focused <input> — a WCAG-adjacent failure (2.4.3/3.2.1-adjacent focus stability) as much as a usability one
- run: "test $(grep -c 'shadowRoot.innerHTML' src/prog-block.js) -gt 0"
- severity: critical
- enforced-by: not yet automated (documentary) — same defect tracked in ../bust/Bustfile.a2ml

## Drift Tolerance

### aaa-claim-creep
- description: No documentation file anywhere in this repo should claim AAA conformance
- tolerance: 0 occurrences of "AAA" in README.md, 0-AI-MANIFEST.a2ml, or .machine_readable/**
- corrective: grep -ril 'AAA' README.md 0-AI-MANIFEST.a2ml .machine_readable/ and remove
- severity: advisory
